+Like `.transform()`, it is strictly unidirectional: a `boolean` carries nothing to reconstruct the input from, so `z.encode()` throws a *runtime error* (not a `ZodError`).
 
-z.encode(successSchema, true);    
+```ts
+z.encode(successSchema, true);
 // ❌ Error: Encountered unidirectional transform during encode: ZodSuccess
-``` */}
+```
 
 
